Richard VanHouten writes:

> > My ascended valkyrie wore a cloak of displacement in the end, but
> > given the choice I would go with the oilskin cloak.

> What's the advantage of the oilskin cloak?

A cloak of displacement protects you from being hit, so it becomes
less useful as the game advances.  An oilskin cloak has maximum magic
cancellation and protects you from grab attacks (most people think
kraken and eels here, and forget owlbears or rope golems holding you
while you would like to run from a pack of orcs).  When exactly the
two break even is certainly debatable and probably depends on play
style.

